MewStage vendor patch multi-host/0002 (third_party/NOTICE): MewUI's AnimationManager was one process-wide instance,
so every embedded host's per-frame pulse (EmbeddedUiHost -> AnimationManager.UpdateAt) ticked EVERY host's
animation clocks, on its own thread: a host on another thread advanced (and raced on) this thread's colour
transitions and paid their allocations. The manager is now per UI thread ([ThreadStatic] instance); a clock keeps
the manager it registered with until it stops, so Stop / Pause / Resume / completion reach the right one. One UI
thread per process (MewUI's own platform hosts) behaves exactly as before. Applies after multi-host/0001.

